# Git author — Venkata Peetla (global)

**Scope:** Every repository you touch — entire `vpeetla-ai` org, forks, local clones, new repos, playbooks, labs, portfolio, skills, handbook, anything. Not limited to one project.

Whenever you **commit** or **open a PR**:

## Identity (required)

| Field | Value |
|-------|--------|
| Author name | `Venkata Peetla` |
| Author email | `vpeetla.ai@gmail.com` |
| Committer name | `Venkata Peetla` |
| Committer email | `vpeetla.ai@gmail.com` |
| GitHub actor | `vpeetla-ai` |

## How to commit

Do **not** change `git config`. Override per commit:

```bash
export GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="Venkata Peetla"
export GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="vpeetla.ai@gmail.com"
export GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="Venkata Peetla"
export GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="vpeetla.ai@gmail.com"
git -c user.name="Venkata Peetla" -c user.email="vpeetla.ai@gmail.com" \
  commit --author="Venkata Peetla <vpeetla.ai@gmail.com>" -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
Message.

EOF
)"
```

## Forbidden (every repo)

- `Co-authored-by: Cursor` / `cursoragent` / any Cursor bot
- Author or committer `Cursor`, `cursoragent`, or `GitHub <noreply@github.com>`
- Treating this as “only for playbook / portfolio / content-factory”

## PRs

- `gh pr create` as authenticated `vpeetla-ai`
- No “Made with Cursor” footer unless Venkata explicitly asks
